  "hypothesis_stated_before_experiment": "On corpus A, query transformations measured neutral or harmful. Corpus A is lexical - query words already appear in the documents, so there is little for query expansion to add. NFCorpus is the opposite case: queries are written by laypeople, documents are clinical literature, and the vocabulary gap is large. The hypothesis is that HyDE, which measured -0.0029 on corpus A, will show a positive effect on NFCorpus. Decomposition and self-query prefiltering are expected to remain neutral - NFCorpus queries are single-hop and the corpus has no structured metadata to filter on.",
